Z||000000||DaveL||05-30-2000||08:29 AM||||Well, this is really quite odd. I had reconnected the original temp guage since the previous owner had disconnected it and added an aftermarket unit to my 87 SE 2.5 DIS, and it was working fine, other than the fact that it reads in degrees centigrade. I let my son use it the other day and when I got back in, there was no more needle for temp.! There is the small round turntable type button that the needle was attached to, and there are two orange dots on it. It does the usual gyrations on startup, then settles down. These two dots seem to line up exactly with the usual temp. range. Are these dots there to show needle direction, or is this just a coincidence?||||reg||6
